# ===== 114.47 Classical Languages Level I =====
H('47.c.1.A',2,"In a Classical Languages class, a student answers either/or and who/what/where/when questions. These are examples of:","simple question-and-answer practice",["advanced literary criticism","map projection","tax forms"],"Level I uses basic question types.")
H('47.c.1.A',2,"Which question is an either/or question?","Is the city on a hill or on the coast?",["What is the city called?","Who founded the city?","When was it built?"],"Either/or questions offer two choices.")
H('47.c.1.B',1,"Memorized greetings in a classical language, such as a simple hello or goodbye, are used in:","basic spoken or written exchanges",["research papers","scientific labs","financial reports"],"Novice learners use memorized phrases.")
H('47.c.1.B',2,"Which is a memorized request a beginner might use?","asking politely for a book",["debating philosophy","composing an epic","analyzing meter"],"Memorized requests are everyday and simple.")
H('47.c.2.A',2,"A Level I student reads a short text adapted from ancient Rome. This is an example of using:","culturally relevant print material",["a periodic table","a math word problem","a weather forecast"],"Adapted texts introduce culture.")
H('47.c.2.A',3,"Which material is culturally relevant to a class studying ancient Greece?","a short passage about daily life in Athens",["a cooking recipe about modern pasta","a sports score","a stock chart"],"Relevant materials connect to the culture studied.")
H('47.c.2.B',2,"After reading a short passage, a Level I student identifies key words and details. This shows:","basic comprehension",["advanced translation of epic poetry","mastery of meter","creative writing"],"Key words and details show understanding.")
H('47.c.2.B',2,"Which is a key detail in a simple story about a Roman market?","what people bought and sold",["the printing press model","the font size","the page number"],"Details come from the story.")
H('47.c.2.C',3,"A learner meets an unfamiliar word in a text with a picture of a temple. The best strategy is to:","use the picture and surrounding words to infer meaning",["skip the passage","guess randomly","stop reading"],"Highly contextualized text allows inference.")
H('47.c.2.C',3,"Many English words come from Latin roots. Knowing this helps a learner:","infer meanings of unfamiliar words",["avoid reading","forget vocabulary","stop studying"],"Roots help inference.")
H('47.c.2.D',2,"A learner sees a picture of a Roman festival in a reading. What does the learner identify?","a cultural practice",["a chemical formula","a geometric proof","a computer program"],"Festivals are cultural practices.")
H('47.c.2.D',3,"Learning how ancient students were taught reading reveals:","a cultural practice of the ancient world",["a science experiment","a modern law","a weather pattern"],"Education practices are cultural.")
H('47.c.3.A',2,"Saying which character in a story you like best is an example of:","expressing a preference",["translating a poem","scanning meter","writing a treaty"],"Preferences are simple opinions.")
H('47.c.3.A',2,"Which sentence expresses a preference?","I prefer the story about the harbor.",["The harbor has twelve docks.","The harbor was built long ago.","Harbors exist."],"Preferences use I prefer or I like.")
H('47.c.3.B',2,"Describing a person in a reading with a mixture of words, phrases and short sentences is:","a simple description",["a complex essay","a meter analysis","a legal brief"],"Novice descriptions combine words and phrases.")
H('47.c.3.B',3,"Which is a simple description of an object in a story?","a tall column made of white stone",["a treatise on columns","an essay on architecture","a debate about stone"],"Simple descriptions use basic details.")

# ===== 114.48 Classical Languages Level II =====
H('48.c.1.A',3,"At Level II, a student answers a question about daily life in Rome and adds a small detail. This is:","simple elaboration",["silence","copying","avoidance"],"Elaboration adds information.")
H('48.c.1.A',3,"Which answer shows simple elaboration to What did the Romans eat?","They ate bread and olives, often with wine.",["Food.","Yes.","I do not know."],"Elaboration adds detail.")
H('48.c.1.B',3,"At Level II, exchanging opinions about a story with simple support includes saying:","I like this character because she is brave.",["Character.","Because.","Brave."],"A reason supports the opinion.")
H('48.c.1.B',3,"Two students trade opinions about a hero from mythology and give a reason. This is:","an exchange of preferences with support",["a dictionary lookup","a spelling drill","a map reading task"],"Preference plus reason.")
H('48.c.1.C',3,"A Level II student tells a classmate what they should do before an exam using an appropriate expression. This is an example of:","giving advice or direction",["describing weather","telling a legend","analyzing a poem"],"Should and must express advice.")
H('48.c.1.C',3,"Which sentence tells someone what they must do?","You must read the passage again.",["The passage is old.","I like the passage.","The passage has a title."],"Must expresses necessity.")
H('48.c.2.A',3,"A learner reads a passage about a Greek theater. The material is described as culturally relevant because it:","connects to the culture being studied",["has no connection","is unrelated to history","is purely fictional"],"Relevance means connection.")
H('48.c.2.A',3,"Which source could be culturally relevant to a Level II classical class?","an adapted passage on a Roman bath",["a modern ad","a sports page","a phone manual"],"Relevant sources relate to the classical world.")
H('48.c.2.B',3,"A theme is:","the central message of a text",["the page number","the author's address","the title font"],"Themes are central ideas.")
H('48.c.2.B',3,"Which task shows identifying main idea and details?","telling what a passage is mostly about and naming two events",["copying the first sentence","counting words","skipping the text"],"Main ideas and details show comprehension.")
H('48.c.2.C',3,"Using context to infer an unfamiliar word in a highly contextualized text means:","looking at nearby words and images for clues",["ignoring the sentence","guessing without clues","stopping"],"Context supports inference.")
H('48.c.2.C',3,"English words such as aquarium and aquatic share a root meaning water. Recognizing this helps a learner:","infer related word meanings",["avoid vocabulary","forget roots","skip reading"],"Word families help inference.")
H('48.c.2.D',3,"From a passage about Greek theater festivals, a learner identifies a cultural practice. This is:","identifying cultural practices",["identifying chemical formulas","identifying tax codes","identifying star charts"],"Festivals are practices.")
H('48.c.2.D',3,"A reading about public baths in Rome shows readers:","how ancient people spent their daily lives",["how to program","how to measure rainfall","how to code"],"Daily life is a cultural practice.")
H('48.c.3.A',3,"Expressing and supporting an opinion about a character means:","giving a reason for the preference",["stating only the name","reading silently","copying a quote"],"Support follows opinion.")
H('48.c.3.A',3,"Which written sentence expresses and supports an opinion?","I think the hero is wise because he listens to advice.",["Hero.","The hero.","Wise."],"A reason supports the opinion.")
H('48.c.3.B',3,"Describing a person or place with essential details means including:","the most important facts",["every possible detail","no detail","unrelated facts"],"Essential details are key facts.")
H('48.c.3.B',3,"Which description includes essential details of a temple?","a marble temple with tall columns on a hill",["a temple","building","a place"],"Details make a description clear.")

# ===== 114.49 Classical Languages Level III =====
H('49.c.1.A',3,"At Level III a student responds to a question on a text with simple elaboration. This shows:","building on a basic answer with added detail",["copying","silence","avoidance"],"Elaboration deepens answers.")
H('49.c.1.A',3,"Which response shows elaboration to a question about a poem's mood?","The mood is sad because the speaker misses home.",["Sad.","Poem.","Yes."],"A reason adds detail.")
H('49.c.1.B',3,"Exchanging opinions about a story with simple support in conversation means:","stating a view and giving a reason",["only reciting a title","avoiding the topic","only copying"],"Support makes opinions stronger.")
H('49.c.1.B',3,"Which statement exchanges a preference with support?","I prefer the epic over the play because the adventure is exciting.",["Epic.","Play.","Adventure."],"Preference plus because.")
H('49.c.1.C',3,"Telling someone what they should do with appropriate expressions is an example of:","giving advice or directions",["describing a map","narrating history","scanning verse"],"Should and must give advice.")
H('49.c.1.C',3,"Which sentence uses an appropriate expression for advice?","You should review the vocabulary before the quiz.",["The vocabulary is a list.","Quiz.","I like vocabulary."],"Should gives advice.")
H('49.c.2.A',4,"Culturally authentic materials in a Level III classical class include:","original or lightly adapted ancient texts",["only textbook exercises","modern slang","unrelated recipes"],"Authentic materials come from the ancient world.")
H('49.c.2.A',4,"Why use authentic texts at Level III?","they show real language and cultural values",["they avoid culture","they replace study","they have no value"],"Authentic texts reflect culture.")
H('49.c.2.B',4,"To paraphrase the main idea of a passage, a learner:","restates it in different words",["copies it exactly","skips it","only underlines"],"Paraphrasing shows understanding.")
H('49.c.2.B',4,"A supporting detail in a passage about a military campaign could be:","a description of the army's route",["the font","the page margin","the paper color"],"Details support the main idea.")
H('49.c.2.C',4,"Analyzing authentic literature for stylistic features includes looking at:","genre, literary devices and the author's choices",["page count only","binding style","font size"],"Style analysis looks at how an author writes.")
H('49.c.2.C',4,"A metaphor in ancient poetry is an example of:","a literary device",["a map symbol","a measurement","a chemical term"],"Metaphors are devices.")
H('49.c.2.D',4,"Inferring the meaning of a new word in a contextualized text relies on:","context and knowledge of word parts",["random guessing","ignoring clues","skipping the sentence"],"Inference uses multiple clues.")
H('49.c.2.D',4,"A learner knows a prefix and a root. Using them to understand a new word is:","a word analysis strategy",["a copying task","a pronunciation drill","a spelling error"],"Word parts help meaning.")
H('49.c.2.E',4,"Comparing how Greeks and Romans celebrated festivals is:","contrasting cultural practices",["comparing math results","measuring angles","naming rivers"],"Practices are compared.")
H('49.c.2.E',4,"A student notes similarities and differences between two ancient cultures' education. This is:","comparing and contrasting cultural practices",["copying vocabulary","ignoring sources","skipping the reading"],"Comparison highlights likeness and difference.")
H('49.c.3.A',4,"Citing justification for an opinion using textual evidence means:","pointing to specific lines or details from the text",["stating a feeling only","repeating the question","avoiding the text"],"Evidence supports an opinion.")
H('49.c.3.A',4,"Which statement uses textual evidence?","The hero is brave because the text says he faces the storm alone.",["The hero is brave.","I like heroes.","Storms exist."],"Evidence from the text supports a claim.")
H('49.c.3.B',4,"Reading poetry aloud with attention to declamation involves:","paying attention to meter, meaning and expression",["reading in a monotone","speeding through","ignoring punctuation"],"Declamation brings out rhythm and meaning.")
H('49.c.3.B',4,"Why does meter matter when reading classical verse aloud?","rhythm shapes the sound and the effect of the poem",["it hides meaning","it is only decoration","it has no effect"],"Meter is central to verse.")
